# Branch test audit: correction tasklist

## Scope and evidence

- Purpose: an implementation contract for maintainers correcting test responsibility, placement, and confirmed defects. This document does not implement those corrections.
- Audited branch: `crafting-menu`, at `95a3d284156b0a7546554fbb393ae908d9edd914`.
- Comparison: `origin/master...HEAD`; merge base `ce97c109caa953085666ad09a797bf49fe81b430`.
- Scope: all 330 test methods in 23 new files, the two added configuration methods, their fixtures, and the changed test-project configuration. Theory rows are additional executions, not additional methods.
- Review: configured `test_reviewer`, using the test-workflow review guidance and actual boundaries rather than folder names.
- Same-reviewer reconciliation assigned all 332 methods once: 123 Unit, 141 Component, 68 Integration, and zero E2E. No test deletion, duplication, or method splitting is required by this disposition.
- Behavioral reference: [Recipe Book design](RecipeBook.md). Existing implementation is evidence, not permission to strengthen its public contract.
- Preserve all existing behavior and unrelated work. Do not remove meaningful coverage merely because it is misclassified or shares a large file.
- Source line references below describe the audited revision. Use method identities when moves change line numbers.

### Confirmed findings

| ID | Priority | Discrepancy | Correction phases |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| F1 | High | Windows-only asset paths in lifecycle and shader tests contradict the supported Ubuntu test configuration. | 2, 6 |
| F2a | Medium | Filter intersection test requires registration-order short-circuiting excluded by the contract. | 2 |
| F2b | Medium | Atomic-publication test injects failure by numbered predicate invocation rather than semantic scenario. | 2 |
| F3 | Medium | Session allocation-reuse test hardcodes allocator-internal native-validation counts. | 2 |
| F4 | Medium | Exact GLSL substring/order checks freeze syntax without proving compilation or rendered behavior. | 5 |
| F5 | Low | Complex added tests lack clear setup/action/assertion phase delineation. | 4 |
| C1 | Organization | Unit/E2E folders and traits misdescribe component and native-integration boundaries. | 1, 3, 6 |
| O1 | Organization | Mixed subjects, levels, and fixture ownership put tests in unrelated files. | 1, 3, 4 |
| O2 | Low | Test project adds an identical second managed `cairo-sharp` reference. | 2 |

### Verification already obtained

- A focused Windows run built successfully: 39 passed, zero failed, zero skipped.
- Selector: `FullyQualifiedName~CraftingNativeTransferTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeFilterSetTests|FullyQualifiedName~RecipeBookToggle_|FullyQualifiedName~ShaderSourceRetainsApprovedPaletteOutlineAndSeparateCornerGeometry|FullyQualifiedName~ExplicitBookOpeningFocusesSearchAndAcceptsTheFirstCharacter`.
- Command shape: `dotnet test .\VanillaExpanded.Tests\VanillaExpanded.Tests.csproj --no-restore --filter "<selector above>" --verbosity minimal`.
- Compilation/analyzer warnings were present. This is not a warning-free-build claim.
- Remaining methods were reviewed statically, not executed.
- No Linux run, live multiplayer workflow, GPU compilation/rendering, or in-game visual acceptance was performed.

## Phase 1 - Establish the placement and discovery contract

Dependencies: none.

- [ ] P1.1 Capture a method-level baseline for all 332 introduced methods, including original fully qualified identity, theory data, category, fixture, collection, and actual tested boundary.
  - [ ] Keep the existing configuration methods outside this branch's additions out of remediation unless fixture extraction directly requires compatibility work.
  - [ ] Use the complete reviewed-file inventory below to ensure no added suite is omitted.
- [ ] P1.2 Establish `Unit`, `Component`, and `Integration` directories and matching category traits within the existing test project.
  - [ ] Unit: an isolated rule/subject; real data objects alone do not automatically make a test component-level.
  - [ ] Component: composed production collaborators exercised behind mocked external services.
  - [ ] Integration: a real native/engine boundary or compatibility contract.
  - [ ] Reserve E2E for a complete externally driven workflow. The seven current native-transfer tests do not qualify.
  - [ ] Do not migrate to a separate test assembly merely to obtain an Integration folder; first preserve internal access, fixtures, and discovery.
- [ ] P1.3 Assign each method exactly one primary responsibility, destination, and level before moving mixed suites.
  - [ ] Follow the responsibility matrix below, including narrow unit cases that must not move wholesale with a mixed file.
  - [ ] Preserve coherent multi-transition lifecycle scenarios when they test one responsibility.
  - [ ] Record any further split needed to distinguish a pure rule from its native compatibility coverage.
- [ ] P1.4 Identify shared fixture ownership and serialization requirements.
  - [ ] Extract `RecipeBookRenderFixture` from the renderer-test file to feature-neutral support when shared GUI tests use it.
  - [ ] Extract common dialog/session fixtures from catch-all suites only where multiple focused suites need them.
  - [ ] Preserve engine-global restoration, disposal, and collection-based serialization.

Exit criteria:
- [ ] Every introduced method has one destination; no method is unassigned or duplicated.
- [ ] Destination names express production responsibility, not the feature that happened to introduce the test.
- [ ] The discovery and serialization contract is explicit before extraction.

## Phase 2 - Correct known test defects without changing feature behavior

Dependencies: Phase 1, so corrected methods retain traceable identities during extraction.

- [ ] P2.1 Fix portable asset lookup (F1).
  - [ ] Replace the three lifecycle fixture asset paths at original lines 3672-3685 in [RecipeBookLifecycleTests.cs](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeBookLifecycleTests.cs).
  - [ ] Replace the shader asset path at original lines 924-927 in [RecipeBookIconRendererTests.cs](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeBookIconRendererTests.cs).
  - [ ] Use platform-portable path segments or deliberately copied test assets; changing only the working directory is insufficient.
  - [ ] Fail explicitly for missing assets rather than skipping or returning successful defaults.
- [ ] P2.2 Correct filter-contract overconstraint (F2a).
  - [ ] Rewrite `ProvidersReceiveTheExactEvaluatedSelectionAndMayShortCircuit`, original lines 73-88 in [RecipeFilterSetTests.cs](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeFilterSetTests.cs).
  - [ ] Preserve exact evaluated-selection identity and intersection-result assertions.
  - [ ] Make providers independently evaluable; do not make a later provider throw solely to enforce registration order or short-circuiting.
- [ ] P2.3 Correct atomic-publication failure injection (F2b).
  - [ ] Rewrite `FailureWhileFilteringStableRecipesDoesNotPublishPartialRows`, original lines 498-520 in [RecipeBookInteractionTests.cs](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeBookInteractionTests.cs).
  - [ ] Fail for a semantically identifiable selection/scenario, not the second predicate call.
  - [ ] Preserve assertions that published rows remain unchanged, no premature notification occurs, and a subsequent valid operation recovers.
  - [ ] Do not require invocation counts that the filtering contract explicitly excludes.
- [ ] P2.4 Decouple session reuse from allocator validation protocol (F3).
  - [ ] Correct `CriteriaChangesReuseAllocationsAndInventoryRefreshEvaluatesExactlyOnce`, original lines 192-233 in [RecipeBookInteractionTests.cs](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/Unit/RecipeBook/RecipeBookInteractionTests.cs).
  - [ ] Retain capture counts and allocation-identity evidence.
  - [ ] Compare criteria-change validation work against a recorded baseline rather than hardcoding native callback totals of two and four.
  - [ ] Keep any justified ordinary/shift native-validation protocol assertions in allocator/native-validation suites, not session reuse tests.
- [ ] P2.5 Remove the duplicate managed Cairo reference (O2).
  - [ ] Remove only the identical duplicate at original lines 83-86 in [VanillaExpanded.Tests.csproj](../VanillaExpanded.Tests/VanillaExpanded.Tests.csproj); preserve the existing reference and native library copying.

Exit criteria:
- [ ] Corrected tests enforce behavioral contracts rather than incidental iteration/validation implementation.
- [ ] No assertion strength is lost merely to make tests pass.
- [ ] Portable asset lookup is ready for actual Windows and Linux execution in Phase 6.

## Phase 3 - Move and split tests by responsibility and boundary

Dependencies: Phases 1 and 2.

The following deterministic mapping supersedes broad file-level classifications. Source selectors refer to attributed test-method declaration lines at `95a3d284`, inclusive, not slices of method bodies. They exclude helpers, constructors, and disposal methods. Move complete methods with every theory-data attribute. Each method belongs to one row only.

Destination files are within the existing test project at `{Level}/{Feature}/{Destination}.cs`. Use `RecipeBook` as the feature unless the row names `Gui/` or `Configuration/`. An unchanged destination name retains the responsibility, not an incorrect original directory. These are planned destinations, not files claimed to exist already.

